<%# locals: (controller:) -%>
<%#
  "PICKED UP WHERE YOU LEFT OFF" (2026-11-24), the one line a kept tool's page shows on the visit
  that handed the tool back as it was left (lib/kept_tools.js). Hidden in the markup and shown by the
  page's keeper, which is `controller`: "addon" on an add-on's page, "keep" on a built-in tool's.
  Both name the same target and the same action, so this is the one spelling of the line.

  START OVER IS THE WAY OUT. Before tools were kept, leaving a tool and coming back was how a maker
  got it fresh; that habit now returns the same tool, so the page has to offer the fresh one itself.
  A quiet link-button, never `primary`: the accent is the top bar's Upload (design-system.md rule 13).

  A PAGE THAT KEEPS A TOOL TAKES NO TURBO PREVIEW, and it says so here because every such page
  renders this partial. A preview is the cached copy of a page, shown while the real one loads. For
  a tool that copy is inert and holds the values of some earlier visit, so a tool about to mount
  fresh (after its 15 minutes, after Start over, for another account in the same tab) would first
  flash what was typed before. Back and Forward still restore from the cache, which is not a preview.
%>
<% content_for :head do %><meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-preview"><% end %>
<%= tag.p class: "tool-resumed muted", role: "status", hidden: true,
          data: { "#{controller}-target": "resumed" } do %>
  Picked up where you left off.
  <%= tag.button "Start over", type: "button", class: "linkbtn", data: { action: "#{controller}#startOver" } %>
<% end %>
